			"Message": "docs(Worker): Overhaul README with architecture tables, caching strategies, and getting-started guide\n\nExpand the README from a brief overview to comprehensive project documentation covering all facets of the Worker service worker component.\n\n**Overview section** — Replace the sparse one-liner with a structured introduction covering the offline-authentication problem statement, caching strategy summary, and a bullet list of the four engineering goals (multi-strategy caching, offline support, dynamic CSS loading, automatic updates).\n\n**Key Features section** — Add detailed descriptions of each caching tier (CORE_CACHE network-first, ASSET_CACHE cache-first), the two-pass CSS loading pipeline, Trusted Types policy enforcement, PostHog+OTLP telemetry bridge, and increment-aware cache keys.\n\n**Core Architecture Principles section** — Introduce a principles table documenting Policy-Based Routing, Build-Time Configuration, CSS Import Interception, Safe Registration, and Observability as the architectural pillars.\n\n**System Architecture section** — Expand the Mermaid diagram with Telemetry bridge, add a connection-paths table documenting protocols (SW API, Cache API, fetch) and use cases between Sky, Worker, Cache Storage, PostHog, and OTLP.\n\n**Project Structure section** — Replace the flat file list with a full tree showing Source, Target (build output), Documentation, Configuration, .github, and root files.\n\n**In the Land Project section** — Add a relationship table with Sky, Wind, and End Users showing the protocol and interaction model.\n\n**Getting Started section** — Add prerequisites (Node.js 18+), build commands (npm install + prepublishOnly), development watch mode, available scripts table, and build-constants reference (__DEV__, __INCREMENT__, BASE_REMOTE).\n\n**Caching Strategies section** — Add a strategy table documenting cache name, URL pattern, and behavior for network-first, cache-first, and pass-through modes, including the increment-based naming scheme.\n\n**API Reference** — Add Worker.ts and Bridge.ts links alongside existing component URLs.\n\n**Related Documentation** — Reorder and expand sister-element descriptions (Sky, Wind, Cocoon).\n\n**Funding section** — Add PlayForm stewardship attribution and restructure funding disclosure.\n\n**Removed sections** — Migrate license and changelog references out of the main README (project-wide files remain available). Drop the Project Maintainers footer block.\n\nStylistic improvements: add em-quad spacing (&#x2001;) before emoji indicators in headings and architecture labels; replace en-dashes with em-dashes for prose breaks; wrap all prose at ~80 characters; standardize code-fence indentation.",
